data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" the source code), **middle-end** (optimizing the code), and **back-end** (generating hardware","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":"-specific machine code). \n\nHere is how a compiler works, stage by stage.\n\n### 1. Lexical Analysis","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" (Scanning)\nThe first stage of the compiler is the lexical analyzer, or \"lexer.\" It takes the raw, unstructured","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" stream of characters in the source file and groups them into meaningful, atomic elements called **tokens**. Tokens include keywords (`if`, `while","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

